    "if_inner_bubble_is_ALE": {
      "rescaled_limit": "for each fixed R, Vol_{r_i^{-2}g_i}(B(x_i,R))/R^4 -> omega_4/|Gamma| (up to ALE asymptotic constants as R grows)",
      "original_scale_translation": "Vol_{g_i}(B(x_i,R r_i)) ~ const*(R r_i)^4 for fixed R",
      "no_immediate_contradiction": "Since R r_i -> 0 for fixed R, this local noncollapse is compatible with total Vol(M_i)->0. Bishop-Gromov permits the volume ratio to decrease on larger radii."
    },
    "what_would_be_needed_to_exclude_top_level_ALE": [
      "a controlled annulus from the ALE end out to a scale comparable with the collapsed ambient scale, with no further curvature concentration and enough Ricci/regularity control to preserve a positive 4-volume ratio",
      "or a proof that the outermost curvature blow-up model must include the collapsed transition in its pointed limit, forcing sub-Euclidean volume growth (ALF/ALG/ALH/AF-like) rather than ALE",
      "or a bubble-tree analysis showing any ALE pieces are strictly inner children of a volume-collapsed parent instanton/transition region, so ADE arithmetic is only a subledger, not the top-level collapse accounting"
    ],
    "corrected_conclusion": "Volume collapse alone does not rule out inner ALE bubbles. It does sharpen the target: the outermost concentration/transition model in a collapsed P4+ sequence should be volume-collapsed at infinity unless a Euclidean-volume-ratio annulus survives. Therefore the ALF/ALG/APS table is central, while the ADE gate remains only a possible inner-bubble diagnostic."
  },
